\DOC DISCHARGE_MEMACCESS_INBOUNDS_USING_ASM_TAC

\TYPE {DISCHARGE_MEMACCESS_INBOUNDS_USING_ASM_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a {memaccess_inbounds} goal by deriving it from a matching
{memaccess_inbounds} assumption in the goal's assumption list.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. It applies to goals whose conclusion is a
{memaccess_inbounds} claim about an event trace together with a list of
readable regions and a list of writable regions, and discharges such a goal
outright:
{
   A ?- memaccess_inbounds t u1 u2
   ================================  DISCHARGE_MEMACCESS_INBOUNDS_USING_ASM_TAC
}
\noindent In the successful observed traces, A always contains a
{memaccess_inbounds} fact whose trace is the same as, or a sub-trace of, the
trace in the conclusion, and whose region lists are covered by those in the
conclusion.

\FAILURE
Fails with a no-match error from an internal {MATCH_MP_TAC} step when the
conclusion's trace cannot be aligned with the available {memaccess_inbounds}
assumption — for instance when the conclusion's trace is an append or cons
wrapping of the assumption's trace in a shape the tactic cannot reduce, or when
the conclusion's region lists do not correspond in the required way to those of
any such assumption. The failure arises inside the tactic itself rather than
from any supplied argument.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this one behaviour — closing such goals — and no
case where the goal is transformed or split.

\ENDDOC
